# Read Project Docs First

Before planning, implementing, or refactoring non-trivial work, read these files in order:

1. **DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md** — engineering standards
2. **PROJECT_CONTEXT.md** — purpose, stack, commands, conventions
3. **CURRENT_STATE.md** — what works, in progress, known issues, blockers
4. **ROADMAP.md** — priorities and planned phases

Also read when relevant:

- **docs/ARCHITECTURE.md** — structure, modules, data flows
- **docs/DECISIONS.md** — past architectural decisions (ADRs)

## When to read

- New session or unfamiliar part of the codebase
- Feature work, non-trivial bug fixes, refactors, dependency changes

## After significant work

- Update **CURRENT_STATE.md** if status or issues changed
- Update **docs/ARCHITECTURE.md** if structure or flows changed
- Add an ADR to **docs/DECISIONS.md** for meaningful technical decisions
- Update **ROADMAP.md** if priorities shifted

Follow **DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md** unless **PROJECT_CONTEXT.md** or an ADR overrides. Prefer minimal, focused changes.
